title: Crates
summary: The workspace's crates, what each holds, and what each depends on.
order: 1
---

<script>
	import CrateMap from '$lib/components/CrateMap.svelte';
</script>

skoro is a workspace of three crates. Each depends only on the crates above it here, and a user
depends on the last, `skoro`, which re-exports the other two. Each crate has a page of its own, which
says what it is for and gives the order in which to read its modules, computed from its sources when
the site is built: an order that uses as little as possible before it is read.

<CrateMap />

| crate          | what it holds                                                                                                                                            |
| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `skoro-tensor` | The layer over burn: the tensor shapes skoro computes with (`Points`, `Frame`, `Integers`, `Value`), each made at an explicit precision on a supported device, the `Target` that names them, and host values. |
| `skoro-core`   | Everything that makes a model a model: [spaces](../../concepts/spaces/) and typed handles, [operations](../../concepts/operations/) and their kernels, the writer and its [scopes](../../concepts/building/), [terms](../../concepts/terms/), [queries](../../concepts/queries/) and the compiler, embedded types, generation and retirement. |
| `skoro`        | The crate a user depends on: it re-exports `skoro-core`, and `skoro-tensor` as `skoro::tensor`, with `Device`, `Precision` and `Target` at its root.     |

No distribution ships yet. What the core leaves for later entries (distributions, the curved types
SO(3) and SE(3), linear algebra, least squares, elimination, serialization and bindings among them)
is listed in the repository's
[`REVISIT.md`](https://github.com/mvarble/skoro/blob/main/REVISIT.md).
